Ze-Reviewed-Against: go.fd.io/govpp v0.13.0

Upstream pull request: none opened yet.

plan/post-release/features/spec-pppoe-vpp-dataplane.md, AC-27, requires:
"Readiness and counter publication are refused. Process retirement requires the
exact retained physical process proof; a claimed PID, logical generation or
another child's completed wait cannot retire a live foreign peer."

Counters must therefore come from the immutable API owner's physical process,
and reconnect cleanup must retain that original process's exact exit proof.
Expose a borrowed callback on the real API dial and real statistics segment
transfer socket, before either becomes usable. Pinned statistics own a single
mapping, with no hidden reconnect to a replacement process. Bound their native
descriptor transfer by the existing configured retry timeout.

Apply after govpp-socket-bounded-close.patch in the canonical sorted patch set.
The API callback uses upstream's existing errors import. Neither callback
transfers socket ownership; callers may retain only a separate kernel process
descriptor.

Design: docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md, "Patching a
vendored module". Deliver through ./le setup install and commit its vendor
result; no compiler overlay or copied client is a delivery route. Delete when
an upstream release provides these contracts.

